"Executioners judge crimes by wizards; judges of the Lower Steps of Recompense do not."
"Tiers run executioner, higher executioner, and Superior Executioner for non-simple crimes."
"Subduers are sent after accused who run or are hurting someone; investigators dig out hidden truths."
"Visitors to an executioner's home spit three times on a heated knife blade."
"The accused is formally called, given about an hour and a half to think, then teleported in."
"Refusing the teleport brings a subduer; false accusers must repay the accused ninefold or more."
"Honesty verification may be requested; a healer's deeper verification cannot be denied."
"Demanding every verification and delay makes the sentence harsher."
"Punishments between a wrist slap and beheading are the norm; beheading if the accused prefers it."
"Executioners may offer 'creative opportunities' sentences, and keep recordings of infamous criminals."
